  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (pca_n2000, singleprofile) achieves 0.485 accuracy while image (resnet50, singleprofile) is only 0.208, making RNA the clearly dominant modality. With only two data points, the most critical uncertainty is whether the RNA representation quality can be improved. Question tested: config_004 changes only the RNA encoder from pca_n2000 (linear) to scvi_n200 (learned nonlinear) while keeping singleprofile constant, giving a clean single-variable comparison against config_001. Why this is the best next step: If scvi_n200 meaningfully outperforms PCA, it establishes that learned representations matter and justifies further encoder exploration (scgpt) and multimodal fusion with a stronger RNA backbone. If it does not improve, it tells us the encoder choice is less impactful than profile structure or fusion strategy, redirecting the search efficiently. This isolates one design axis without confounding changes, maximizing information per experiment under the limited budget."
